# Build output.
#
# The binary lands at the repo root (see the Makefile), so the pattern is
# root-anchored. An unanchored `sixi-scanner` line would also match
# cmd/sixi-scanner/ and silently exclude the entire main package from the
# repository, which is exactly what it did once.
#
# Guard: after editing this file, `git ls-files cmd/` must list the main
# package, and `go build ./...` must still work.
/sixi-scanner
/sixi-scanner.exe
/dist/
*.exe

# Reports produced by local runs. These contain whatever the target disclosed,
# which is exactly the kind of thing that must not end up in a commit.
*.sarif
*.json.report
/report.json
/sixi.sarif
scan-report.*
out/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
